/* book exam traps: Sizing the bolts for the seating load only. They must carry the larger of Wm1 and Wm2; in the example the pressure case (189.9 kN) governs. | Using the outside diameter for G. For a narrow gasket (b₀ ≤ 6.4 mm) G is the mean diameter of the gasket. | Forgetting the factor 2π in Hp = 2π b G m p, or putting b = N instead of b₀ = N/2. | Thinking more O-ring squeeze is always better. Too much squeeze, or a groove filled above about 85 %, overloads the rubber and it cracks or extrudes. | Fitting a lip seal with its lip facing away from the oil. The lip must face the fluid it holds back. */
